# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Development is on Windows; every deployment target is Linux. Without this, git checks
# out CRLF locally, and the type-B artifacts — scripts/backup.sh (PH-0.28), the Dockerfiles
# (PH-0.10) — are COPYed into a container with CRLF endings, where `#!/bin/bash\r` is not
# a valid interpreter path. The failure appears only in the container, never locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary

pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated -diff
